OL,3,GNEWSAHorse visits hospice to say final 
OL,4,Agoodbye                                
OL,6,FWakefield Hospice is used to           
OL,7,Faccommodating four-legged friends      
OL,8,Fvisiting patients.                     
OL,10,FBut when one man asked to see a horse  
OL,11,Ffor the final time, it threw up a      
OL,12,Fslightly higher logistical hurdle for  
OL,13,Fstaff.                                 
OL,15,FThe man's family, who wish to remain   
OL,16,Fanonymous, arranged to bring Rudy the  
OL,17,Fhorse from Tadcaster, while hospice    
OL,18,Fstaff reserved a parking spot for the  
OL,19,Ftrailer and moved their patient to be  
OL,20,Fcloser to the creature.                
OL,23,APub: 21-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
